diff --git a/docs/decisions/1138-react-compiler-compatible-closures-and-handles.md b/docs/decisions/1138-react-compiler-compatible-closures-and-handles.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8cf3094
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/1138-react-compiler-compatible-closures-and-handles.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# React Compiler compatible closures and mutable handles
+
+Status: downstream consumer fix. Date: 2026-11-14.
+
+## Findings
+
+A Rust browser application enabled React Compiler with the official Vite React
+plugin. Three generated forms prevented automatic optimization: a promoted named
+callback whose body shadows its name (#1702), reassignment of a parameter for a
+new Rust shadow binding (#1705), and inline accessor objects for mutable places
+inside a custom hook (#1703). Each is valid JavaScript; these findings do not
+claim a Rust semantic wrong answer.
+
+## Decision
+
+Keep lexical arrows where promotion would introduce a self-name declared inside
+the callback. Keep a copied-object parameter shadow as a new JavaScript local. Copy lowering
+records the fresh-copy fact, which shadowing consumes rather than guessing from
+JavaScript shapes. Primitive shadows keep existing readable reuse; explicit
+Rust mutation remains mutation, and ordinary local reuse remains available.
+
+The mutable-place representation owns the runtime constructor name. Linking
+registers it before preparation; preparation supplies lexical reader/writer
+closures that retain its existing storage conversions. The existing handle
+runtime owns accessor construction, also used by computed-property handles.
+Construction does not invoke the reader or writer. Handles remain fresh objects;
+get/set behavior, dictionary presence and key order are preserved.
+
+For ADR 0262, all three decisions follow the **no observable Rust difference**
+case. They change emitted form while retaining copying, aliasing, root
+replacement, side-effect ordering and panics. No unsafe optimizer assumptions or
+application-side rewrites are introduced.
+
+## Proof and consumer contract
+
+The four regressions in `test/react-compiler-output.test.ts` fail against the
+old output and pass with this change. JSON root replacement and nested mutation
+are compared with native Rust; cloned object parameters retain source identity
+and values. Existing cell, serde value, function and standard-library tests cover
+the affected boundaries. The consumer also runs the actual React Compiler on its
+generated App, Icon and WebMCP hook, verifies memoization and no diagnostics, then
+runs pixel-level browser tests with optimization enabled.
+
+The declaration-form code was extracted from the oversized preparation module
+before extending it. It has one preparation owner; handle dependency ownership
+is represented explicitly rather than reconstructed from printed JavaScript.
+
+The readability baseline is regenerated after all snapshots. Independent copied
+parameters deliberately retain their Rust shadow as a fresh local; the small
+renamed-local increase is necessary for automatic optimization. Moving accessor
+objects into the shared runtime also changes generated line counts, so unrelated
+shape shares can move without introducing another instance.
