@@ -457,3 +457,13 @@ note: found an item that was configured out
     | #[cfg(react = "19.2")]
     |       -------------- the item is gated behind the `19.2` feature
 ```
+
+## Automatic React optimization
+
+Rust-authored components and hooks can pass through React Compiler after rust-js
+emits JavaScript. Configure the host's React integration once; no manual memoization
+or hand edits to generated code are needed. Object-copy parameter shadows remain distinct
+locals and mutable-place accessors use the runtime constructor, so idiomatic Rust
+can be analyzed by React Compiler. Verify actual optimization in the host, rather
+than treating a successful bundle as proof that every component was optimized.
+See [the decision](../../decisions/1138-react-compiler-compatible-closures-and-handles.md).
